{
  "comment": "Cross-language dock-address contract. Asserted by tests/unit/test_dock_address_contract.py (Python: flow_sdk/core/dock_address.py) and ui/tests/unit/dock-address-contract.test.ts (TypeScript: ts_sdk/src/utils/ui/view-types.ts, ts_sdk/src/utils/ui/retired-views.ts, ui/src/types/ViewType.ts, ui/src/navigation/DockPointer.ts, ui/src/navigation/url-builder.ts). NEITHER SIDE GENERATES THIS FILE: it is an independent third statement, so an edit to one language fails the OTHER language's suite. Editing only this file fails both, which is the signal that a paired change is needed. OUT OF SCOPE, deliberately: (1) tab-identity STRINGS -- DockPointer.tabHash is the single canonicalizer and the backend stores its output as an opaque uuid5 key, so only its NULL-NESS is pinned here (tab_identity_cases.tab_hash null vs non-null); the string column is asserted by the TypeScript side alone. (2) Viewer chrome (title / iconName / tabLocation / canAddAsTab), which no backend caller reads. Every `options` value below is restricted to [A-Za-z0-9._-] so the two languages' query-string encoders cannot diverge on a character no caller uses. url_cases defaults when a key is omitted: layout='dock', page='desk', options={}, base='', pointer=null.",
